# ARS Paper Day Theme

Use the ARS Paper Day design system for new or updated frontend UI.

- Use semantic variables from `src/styles/ars-tokens.css`; do not add arbitrary color literals in component CSS.
- Primary actions and selected states use `--accent-primary` with `--ink-primary` text. Never use white text on yellow.
- Keep normal surfaces white or warm white (`--surface-raised`, `--surface-paper`, `--app-canvas`), with near-black ink (`--ink-primary`) for high-emphasis text.
- Use `--accent-hover` for hover states and `--focus-ring` for visible keyboard focus.
- Preserve paired semantic status tokens for success, warning, danger, and information. Yellow is not a substitute for status feedback.
- Use `--font-family-serif` for page and modal headings; use `--font-family-ui` for interface controls and body text.
- Use `--border-subtle` and `--border-strong` for structure rather than arbitrary gray borders.
- Every interactive element needs hover, disabled, and `:focus-visible` states. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

```css
/* Correct: semantic Paper Day action */
.primaryButton {
  background: var(--accent-primary);
  color: var(--ink-primary);
  border: 1px solid var(--accent-primary);
}

/* Avoid: hard-coded blue or white-on-yellow action text */
```
